concept:privacy-amendment-office-of-the-privacy-commissioner-act-2000-sch-1-sec-26a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26A Staff and consultants"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26a ;
    values:originalText "(1) The staff necessary to assist the Commissioner must be persons appointed or employed under the Public Service Act 1922.  (2) The Commissioner has all the powers of, or exercisable by, a Secretary under that Act, so far as those powers relate to the branch of the Australian Public Service comprising the staff mentioned in subsection (1), as if that branch were a separate Department of the Australian Public Service.  Office of the Privacy Commissioner  Schedule 1 Privacy Act 1988  Part 1  Privacy Amendment (Office of the Privacy Commissioner) Act 2000                   3  (3) The Commissioner may engage as consultants persons with suitable qualifications and experience. The terms and conditions on which a consultant is engaged are as determined by the Commissioner." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The staff necessary to assist the Commissioner must be persons appointed or employed under the Public Service Act 1922.  (2) The Commissioner has all the powers of, or exercisable by, a Secretary under that Act, so far as those powers relate to the branch of the Australian Public Service comprising the staff mentioned in subsection (1), as if that branch were a separate Department of the Australian Public Service.  Office of the Privacy Commissioner  Schedule 1 Privacy Act 1988  Part 1  Privacy Amendment (Office of the Privacy Commissioner) Act 2000                   3  (3) The Commissioner may engage as consultants persons with suitable qualifications and experience. The terms and conditions on which a consultant is engaged are as determined by the Commissioner."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "347d135b6521dcd27b991f7e0eb0e817cb5f5b580793467e1252561976851657" ;
    cof:pageNumber "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-office-of-the-privacy-commissioner-act-2000-sch-1-sec-26a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-office-of-the-privacy-commissioner-act-2000-sch-1-sec-26a-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-office-of-the-privacy-commissioner-act-2000-sch-1-sec-26a-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-office-of-the-privacy-commissioner-act-2000.pdf> ;
    dc:source "privacy-amendment-office-of-the-privacy-commissioner-act-2000.pdf, p.6" .
doc:sch-1-sec-26a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26A Staff and consultants" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The staff necessary to assist the Commissioner must be persons appointed or employed under the Public Service Act 1922.  (2) The Commissioner has all the powers of, or exercisable by, a Secretary under that Act, so far as those powers relate to the branch of the Australian Public Service comprising the staff mentioned in subsection (1), as if that branch were a separate Department of the Australian Public Service.  Office of the Privacy Commissioner  Schedule 1 Privacy Act 1988  Part 1  Privacy Amendment (Office of the Privacy Commissioner) Act 2000                   3  (3) The Commissioner may engage as consultants persons with suitable qualifications and experience. The terms and conditions on which a consultant is engaged are as determined by the Commissioner." ;
    cof:pageNumber "6"^^xsd:integer .

